thru
Contact
City Engineer
 Description
This project would replace the approach slabs and epoxy coat the deck of the bridge on Westland Road crossing Crow Creek (Structure FRZ).  In
the last biennial bridge inspection, WYDOT identified that the concrete on the approach slabs is delaminating.  Further investigation in the spring
of 2016 revealed that approximately 50% of the area of the approach slabs is separating and will likely fail with additional freeze/thaw cycles.
Additionally, the rebar in the bridge deck shows signs of rusting and needs to be sealed against additional water infiltration.
Project #
EN-16-013
 Justification
Postponing repairs will likely result in more extensive repairs being needed later.
